{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"agent_message","text":"The low-level tests found a real ground-truth sensitivity: GCC `-O3` changes results because the C arithmetic contains signed-overflow/shift undefined behavior. The original CMake build is unoptimized and earlier matched Rust exactly, so I’m reverting the differential `.so` to the default `-O0` semantics and checking whether any conservative optimization level preserves those bytes before addressing runtime."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for opt in 0 1 2 3; do cc -O$opt -fPIC -shared -o build/libdriver_c_O$opt.so src/main.c; done\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport ctypes\nn=262144\nfor name in ['O0','O1','O2','O3']:\n d=ctypes.CDLL(f'./build/libdriver_c_{name}.so')\n a=(ctypes.c_int*n).in_dll(d,'array')\n x=1\n for i in range(n):\n  x=(x*1664525+1013904223)&0xffffffff\n  a[i]=ctypes.c_int32(x).value\n d.perform_expensive_operations()\n print(name, list(a[:5]), sum((v&0xffffffff) for v in a)&0xffffffffffffffff)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
